==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|is|gel}}
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|kaldr|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*kaldaz}}, ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*gel-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkʰaltʏr/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|altʏr|lang=is}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj|kaldari|kaldastur}}

# {{context|of a thing|lang=is}} [[cold]]; having a [[low]] [[temperature]]
#: '''''Kalt''' járn.''
#:: '''Cold''' iron.
#: ''Mér er '''kalt''' á höndunum.''
#:: My hands are '''cold'''.
# {{context|of the weather|lang=is}} [[cold]]; causing the [[air]] to be [[cold]]
# [[cold]]; [[unfriendly]], [[emotional]]ly distant or [[unfeeling]] 
#: '''''Köld''' augu.''
#:: '''Cold''' eyes.
#: '''''Kaldur''' svipur.''
#:: A '''cold''' look.
# [[cool]], [[calm]]

